Article 1 (Purpose) The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Railroad Enterprise Act and matters necessary for its enforcement.

Article 2 (Railroad-Related Statutes) "Railroad-related statutes prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 1 (c) and (d) of Article 7 of the Railroad Enterprise Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") each means the following statutes: <Amended on June 28, 2016; September 10, 2020>
1. The Framework Act on the Development of Railroad Industry;
2. The Railroad Safety Act;
3. The Urban Railroad Act;
4. The Korea National Railway Act;
5. The Korea Railroad Corporation Act.

Article 3 (Reporting of Passenger Fares and Charges)
(1) Where a railroad business operator intends to report fares and charges for passengers (hereinafter referred to as "passenger fares and charges") or report a change thereto pursuant to Article 9 (1) of the Act, the operator shall submit to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport a report on passenger fares and charges or a report on a change thereto prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, accompanied by the following documents: <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013; June 28, 2016>
1. A schedule of passenger fares and charges;
2. A comparison table of the new and former passenger fares and charges and a document stating the reasons for the change (limited to cases where passenger fares and charges are changed).
(2) Where a railroad business operator intends to operate a commercial railroad in connection with an urban railroad operated by an urban railroad operator under the Urban Railroad Act, the operator shall consult in advance with the relevant urban railroad operator regarding passenger fares and charges and the timing of changes thereto before reporting passenger fares and charges or a change thereto pursuant to Article 9 (1) of the Act. <Amended on July 7, 2014; June 28, 2016>

Article 4 (Designation of Ceilings on Passenger Fares, Etc.)
(1) When designating a ceiling on fares for passengers (hereinafter referred to as "passenger fares") pursuant to the latter part of Article 9 (2) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall take into account the rate of inflation, cost levels, equity with other modes of transport, the classification of commercial railroad lines under Article 4 (2) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "commercial railroad lines"), the types of rolling stock under Article 4-2 of the Act, etc., and, where a ceiling on passenger fares has been designated, shall publicly notify it in the Official Gazette. <Amended on February 29, 2008; June 25, 2008; March 23, 2013; June 28, 2016>
(2) To designate a ceiling on passenger fares pursuant to paragraph (1), the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may hear the opinions of the Railroad Industry Committee under Article 6 of the Framework Act on the Development of Railroad Industry, or specialized institutions and experts related to railroads or transport. <Amended on June 28, 2016>
(3) Deleted <Deleted on October 20, 2008>
(4) Deleted <Deleted on October 20, 2008>
(5) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport intends to designate a ceiling on passenger fares, the Minister may require railroad business operators to submit documents stating cost calculations and other bases for calculating passenger fares. <Amended on February 29, 2008; June 25, 2008; March 23, 2013; June 28, 2016>
(6) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport designates a ceiling on passenger fares under paragraph (1) for a section in which commercial railroad lines and urban railroads under the Urban Railroad Act are connected and operated, the Minister shall ensure that the ceiling is in harmony with the range of urban railroad fares determined by the Special Metropolitan City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayor, Special Self-Governing City Mayor, Do Governor, or Special Self-Governing Province Governor pursuant to Article 31 (1) of the Urban Railroad Act. <Amended on February 29, 2008; June 25, 2008; March 23, 2013; July 7, 2014; June 28, 2016>

Article 5 (Changes to Important Matters in Business Plans) "Where intending to change important matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 12 (1) of the Act means any of the following cases: <Amended on June 25, 2008; June 28, 2016>
1. Where the type of railroad transport service (meaning railroad passenger transport service or railroad freight transport service) is changed or another type of railroad transport service is added for a remote line on which extremely low demand for railroad use makes it very difficult to achieve a balance between revenue and expenditure and for which a contract for compensation of public service costs has been concluded pursuant to Article 33 (1) of the Framework Act on the Development of Railroad Industry;
2. A change in the section of operation (limited to passenger trains);
3. Where stopping stations for passenger trains are newly established, abolished, or changed by at least 2/10 for each commercial railroad line;
4. A change of at least 1/10 in the number of services for each commercial railroad line (limited to passenger trains): Provided, That cases where the number of services is changed for a period of not more than three months due to a substantial difference between transport demand and the transport capacity under the train operation plan, such as during public holidays or school vacation periods, shall be excluded.

Article 6 (Criteria for Railroad Accidents for Which Changes to Business Plans May Be Restricted) "Criteria prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 12 (2) 4 of the Act means where, in the year immediately preceding the year in which an application for a change to a business plan is filed, the number of deaths caused by railroad accidents (meaning railroad accidents caused by an intentional act or negligence of a railroad business operator or its employees; hereinafter the same shall apply) per one million kilometers of train operation or the number of railroad accidents per one million kilometers of train operation has increased by at least 2/10 over the average for the most recent five years (excluding the immediately preceding year). <Amended on June 25, 2008; June 28, 2016>

Article 7 (Posting of Details of Suspension or Closure of Business) Where a railroad business operator obtains permission to suspend or close its railroad business pursuant to Article 15 (1) of the Act, the operator shall, within seven days from the date on which permission is obtained, post the following matters on the railroad business operator's website and at relevant stations, sales offices, business offices, and other places readily visible to the general public pursuant to Article 15 (4) of the Act: Provided, That where a suspension is reported pursuant to the proviso to Article 15 (1) of the Act, the following matters shall be posted immediately upon the occurrence of the relevant ground: <Amended on June 28, 2016>
1. The details of the railroad business to be suspended or closed and the reasons therefor;
2. In the case of suspension, its period;
3. Guidance on alternative means of transport;
4. Where the railroad business operator recognizes that there are other matters related to the suspension or closure that need to be made known to the public, those matters.

Article 8 (Number of Casualties Subject to Dispositions Such as Revocation of License or Suspension of Business) "Where a large number of casualties prescribed by Presidential Decree occurs" in Article 16 (1) 3 of the Act means where at least five deaths occur in a single railroad accident. <Amended on June 25, 2008; June 28, 2016>

Article 9 (Criteria for Imposition of Penalty Surcharges on Railroad Business Operators) The amounts of penalty surcharges according to the types and severity of violations for which a penalty surcharge is imposed in lieu of a disposition of suspension of business pursuant to Article 17 (1) of the Act shall be as specified in attached Table 1.

Article 10 (Imposition and Payment of Penalty Surcharges)
(1) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport intends to impose a penalty surcharge pursuant to Article 17 (1) of the Act, the Minister shall give written notice requiring its payment, specifying the type of violation, the amount of the relevant penalty surcharge, etc. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
(2) A person who receives notice pursuant to paragraph (1) shall pay the penalty surcharge to a collecting institution designated by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport within 20 days: Provided, That where the person is unable to pay the penalty surcharge within that period due to a natural disaster or other unavoidable cause, the person shall pay it within seven days from the date on which that cause ceases to exist. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
(3) A collecting institution that receives payment of a penalty surcharge pursuant to paragraph (2) shall issue a receipt to the payer.
(4) Where a collecting institution for penalty surcharges receives a penalty surcharge pursuant to paragraph (2), it shall notify the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport of that fact without delay. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
(5) Deleted <Deleted on September 24, 2021>

Article 10-2 (Criteria for Imposition of Penalty Surcharges on Privately Financed Railroad Business Operators) The criteria for imposition, such as the amounts of penalty surcharges according to the types and severity of violations, etc. for which a penalty surcharge is imposed pursuant to Article 25-2 (1) of the Act, shall be as specified in attached Table 1-2.

Article 10-3 (Imposition and Payment of Penalty Surcharges) Article 10 shall apply mutatis mutandis to the imposition and payment of penalty surcharges on privately financed railroad business operators under Article 25 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "privately financed railroad business operators"). In such cases, "Article 17 (1) of the Act" shall be construed as "Article 25-2 (1) of the Act."

Article 10-4 (Requests for Changes to Concession Agreements Due to Changes in Circumstances, Etc.)
(1) "Criteria prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 25-3 (1) 1 of the Act means the ratio of equity capital that a privately financed railroad business operator must maintain in accordance with the master plan for private investment projects under Article 7 of the Act on Public-Private Partnerships in Infrastructure.
(2) "Interest rate exceeding the criteria prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 25-3 (1) 2 of the Act means an interest rate exceeding the lowest of the following interest rates:
1. The interest rate under Article 5 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on Registration of Credit Business and Protection of Finance Users;
2. The maximum interest rate under the Regulations on the Maximum Interest Rate under Article 2 (1) of the Interest Limitation Act;
3. Where there is an agreement with the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport on the maximum interest rate when a privately financed railroad business operator borrows funds, that interest rate.
(3) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 25-3 (1) 3 of the Act means where, after a concession agreement under subparagraph 7 of Article 2 of the Act on Public-Private Partnerships in Infrastructure (hereinafter referred to as a "concession agreement" in this paragraph) is concluded, annual actual traffic volume changes by at least 30/100 of the traffic volume stipulated in the concession agreement due to any of the following cases:
1. Where another railroad whose connection was not anticipated at the time of conclusion of the concession agreement for the relevant privately financed railroad is connected;
2. Where a change in the operating conditions of the relevant privately financed railroad seriously impairs the functions of the privately financed railroad, such as user safety and convenience;
3. Where the relevant privately financed railroad is included within the scope established for an impact area of an interconnected transport system under Article 36 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the National Transport System Efficiency Act;
4. Where relevant statutes are amended or policies concerning privately financed railroads are changed;
5. Where transport conditions change substantially due to other grounds equivalent to those referred to in subparagraphs 1 through 4.

Article 11 (Publication of Evaluation Results)
(1) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport publishes the results of a quality evaluation of railroad services pursuant to Article 27 of the Act, the following matters shall be included: <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
1. The evaluation results for each evaluation indicator;
2. The degree of improvement in the quality of railroad services;
3. The ranking of each railroad business operator in the evaluation;
4. Other matters that the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport deems necessary to publish as a result of the quality evaluation of railroad services.
(2) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may implement support measures, including awards, within budgetary limits for railroad business operators and their employees whose railroad services receive excellent quality evaluation results. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>

Article 12 (Minor Changes to Registered Matters concerning Exclusive Railroads, etc.)
(1) “Cases of minor changes prescribed by Presidential Decree” in the proviso to Article 34 (1) of the Act means any of the following cases: <Amended on June 28, 2016>
1. Where operating hours are extended or shortened;
2. Where dispatch intervals or the number of services are reduced or increased;
3. Where the number of railroad vehicles is changed within a range of 1/10;
4. Where ancillary facilities related to transportation, other than the principal office and railroad vehicle depot, are changed;
5. Where officers are changed (limited to corporations);
6. Where the construction period of an exclusive railroad is adjusted within a range of six months.
(2) Where an exclusive railroad operator suspends or discontinues all or part of the operation of an exclusive railroad pursuant to Article 38 of the Act, the operator shall take the following measures: <Amended on June 28, 2016>
1. Measures to prevent the suspension or discontinuance from impeding railroad operation or the safety of railroad operation;
2. Measures to prevent the suspension or discontinuance from aggravating natural disasters, environmental pollution, or the like.

Article 13 (Application for Permission for Occupancy and Use and Term of Permission)
(1) A person who intends to obtain permission for occupancy and use of railroad facilities owned and managed by the State pursuant to Article 42 (1) of the Act shall submit to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport an application for permission for occupancy and use prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, accompanied by the following documents. In such cases, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall verify the certificate of registered corporate matters (limited to corporations) through the joint use of administrative information under Article 36 (1) of the Electronic Government Act. <Amended on February 29, 2008; November 2, 2010; March 23, 2013>
1. Documents outlining the project;
2. Documents concerning plans for the construction and use of facilities;
3. Documents concerning the financing plan;
4. Documents concerning projections of income and expenditure;
5. In the case of a corporation, its articles of incorporation;
6. Design documents for the facilities to be installed (meaning specifications, a location map, floor plans, and principal cross-sectional drawings);
7. Other documents stating relevant information.
(2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport intends to grant permission for occupancy and use of railroad facilities owned and managed by the State pursuant to Article 42 (1) of the Act, the term of permission shall not exceed the respective periods in the following subparagraphs. Provided, That where a building or other facility is to be installed, the period required for its construction shall not be counted. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013; October 10, 2023>
1. Where the purpose is to construct a steel-frame, reinforced-concrete, masonry, or other similarly durable building: 50 years;
2. Where the purpose is to construct a building other than those under subparagraph 1: 15 years;
3. Where the purpose is to construct a structure other than a building: Five years.
(3) Deleted. <Deleted on October 10, 2023>

Article 14 (Occupancy and Use Fees)
(1) Occupancy and use fees under Article 44 (1) of the Act shall be calculated on the basis of the value of the railroad facilities for which permission for occupancy and use is to be granted and the sales of the business conducted under that permission; detailed standards for calculating occupancy and use fees shall be determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
(2) The value of railroad facilities under paragraph (1) shall be calculated by applying Article 42 of the Enforcement Decree of the State Property Act mutatis mutandis; the value so calculated shall apply only for a period of up to three years after its calculation. <Amended on July 27, 2009>
(3) Reductions of or exemptions from occupancy and use fees under Article 44 (2) of the Act shall be as specified in the following subparagraphs: <Added on June 25, 2019; amended on October 10, 2023>
1. In cases falling under Article 44 (2) 1 and 2 of the Act: Occupancy and use fees shall be reduced or exempted in proportion to the facilities to be transferred or provided to the State without compensation out of all the facilities;
2. In cases falling under Article 44 (2) 3 of the Act: Occupancy and use fees for the site of the relevant railroad facilities shall be reduced or exempted in accordance with standards prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport;
3. In cases falling under Article 44 (2) 4 of the Act: Occupancy and use fees shall be reduced or exempted as specified in the following items:
(a) Where all of the facilities for which permission for occupancy and use has been granted could not be used: The full amount of occupancy and use fees for the relevant period shall be exempted;
(b) Where part of the facilities for which permission for occupancy and use has been granted could not be used: Occupancy and use fees for the relevant period shall be reduced in proportion to the area of the facilities that could not be used out of the total area for which permission for occupancy and use was granted.
(4) Occupancy and use fees for the relevant year shall be paid in advance by the end of January each year. Provided, That where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport deems advance payment difficult for unavoidable reasons, the Minister may set a separate payment deadline. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013; June 25, 2019>

Article 15 (Transfer of Rights and Obligations)
(1) Where a person who has obtained permission for occupancy and use pursuant to Article 42 of the Act intends to obtain authorization for the transfer of the person's rights and obligations pursuant to Article 45 of the Act, the person shall submit to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, no later than three months before the intended date of transfer of the rights and obligations, an application prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, accompanied by the following documents: <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
1. A copy of the transfer agreement;
2. A detailed statement of the transfer price.
(2) Where rights and obligations arising from permission for occupancy and use of railroad facilities are transferred with authorization from the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport pursuant to Article 45 of the Act, the term of permission for occupancy and use for the transferee of those rights and obligations shall be the remaining term of the permission for occupancy and use granted to the transferor. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>

Article 16 (Duty to Restore to Original Condition)
(1) A person who has obtained permission for occupancy and use of railroad facilities pursuant to Article 42 (1) of the Act shall restore the railroad facilities for which the permission was granted to their original condition within three months from the date on which the term of permission for occupancy and use expires or the occupancy and use is discontinued. Provided, That the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may extend the period for restoration where deemed unavoidable. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
(2) Where a person who has obtained permission for occupancy and use intends to be exempted from the duty to restore all or part of the relevant railroad facilities to their original condition pursuant to the proviso to Article 46 (1) of the Act, notwithstanding expiration of the term of permission or discontinuance of occupancy and use, the person shall submit an application stating the reasons to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport no later than three months before the expiration date of the term of permission for occupancy and use or the date of discontinuance of occupancy and use. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
(3) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport receives an application for exemption from a person who has obtained permission for occupancy and use under paragraph (2), or intends ex officio to exempt that person from the duty to restore all or part of the railroad facilities to their original condition, the Minister shall notify the person who has obtained permission for occupancy and use in writing, specifying the portion for which the duty of restoration is exempted, by the expiration date of the term of permission for occupancy and use or the date of discontinuance of occupancy and use. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>

Article 16-2 (Processing of Sensitive Information and Personally Identifiable Information)
Where unavoidable for the performance of any of the following duties, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may process information constituting criminal history records under subparagraph 2 of Article 18 of the Enforcement Decree of the Personal Information Protection Act, or materials containing resident registration numbers, passport numbers, or alien registration numbers under Article 19, subparagraph 1, 2, or 4 of that Decree: <Amended on March 23, 2013>
1. Duties concerning licenses under Article 5 of the Act;
2. Duties concerning the transfer and acquisition of businesses, etc. under Article 14 of the Act;
3. Duties concerning the revocation of licenses, etc. under Article 16 of the Act;
4. Duties concerning the registration of exclusive railroads under Article 34 of the Act;
5. Duties concerning the transfer and acquisition of the operation of exclusive railroads, etc. under Article 36 of the Act;
6. Duties concerning succession to the operation of exclusive railroads by inheritance under Article 37 of the Act;
7. Duties concerning revocation of the registration of exclusive railroads under Article 40 of the Act.

Article 16-3 Deleted. <Deleted on December 24, 2018>

Article 17 (Criteria for Imposing Administrative Fines)
The criteria for imposing administrative fines under Article 51 (1) through (4) of the Act shall be as specified in attached Table 2.

