Article 3 (Special Cases concerning Number of Extensions of Periods of Permission for Occupancy and Use of Railroad Facilities)
Where a person who, as at the time this Decree enters into force, has obtained permission for occupancy and use or an extension of the period of permission for occupancy and use for the purpose specified in Article 13 (2) 1 has an unexpired period of permission for occupancy and use, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may extend that period on one occasion only, unless there are special grounds, taking into consideration the condition of the facilities, operating performance, etc., notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 13 (3). In such cases, the extension period shall not exceed 20 years.

Article 4 (Transitional Measures concerning Period of Permission for Occupancy and Use for Steel-Framed Buildings, etc.)
Where a person who, as at the time this Decree enters into force, has obtained permission for occupancy and use or an extension of the period of permission for occupancy and use for the purpose specified in former Article 13 (2) 1 has an unexpired period of permission for occupancy and use, the former provisions shall apply to that period of permission for occupancy and use, notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 13 (2) 1.
